{"id": "EUVD-2026-103864", "enisaUuid": "c3a85da5-9de5-32e7-8d61-e85fcbbd10bd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: fix ACP MFD device leak on init failure\n\nacp_hw_init() registers ACP child devices with mfd_add_devices() before\nattaching them to the ACP power domain and initializing the hardware.\n\nIf attaching a child to the power domain fails, or if the ACP reset or\nclock enable operation times out, the failure path frees only the\nsource cell, resource, and platform-data allocations. The child\nplatform devices already registered by mfd_add_devices() remain\nregistered and are never released.\n\nRemove the children from the power domain and unregister the MFD\ndevices on failures that occur after mfd_add_devices() succeeds. Keep\nmfd_add_devices() failures on the existing cleanup path since the MFD\ncore already rolls back partially registered children itself.\n\nThe issue was identified by a static analysis tool I developed and\nconfirmed by manual review.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 63da68d6a2279ec945581c990c5a59a5ae8b5560)", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d700c26ed64bd3c26e4aa7679b9d5f3333c3747a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b9a53940a2bc063ea4cd09ee49220a503a0170c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/587469076e4ffb617f7ad1a0c4a13072a3e87113", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abf854513bc19e6e24d45353ac99ec5627ee0acc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0013046151b7467e62c471c1c83d63ea255799c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7q7p-f6vv-qrwf", "CVE-2026-98779"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e35f5d8-a95e-3fd3-aa99-b6977a3c5099", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "2ca33f09-17a8-3fdd-bace-2dc638e1b6c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "47ca72f3-d7f9-3a82-a263-7fd19b388eb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25030321ba2860c56651429a4f28d94a6483d952 <587469076e4ffb617f7ad1a0c4a13072a3e87113"}, {"id": "484991d1-2a0a-3652-ade6-424b0f86a479", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25030321ba2860c56651429a4f28d94a6483d952 <2b9a53940a2bc063ea4cd09ee49220a503a0170c"}, {"id": "5ae810df-5151-37ce-aaed-31034d1ffc7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5c60ac91-fd83-31c6-83be-6f48434f92e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25030321ba2860c56651429a4f28d94a6483d952 <d700c26ed64bd3c26e4aa7679b9d5f3333c3747a"}, {"id": "5eeda36d-79e2-3d22-80c9-fb5bcca037d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25030321ba2860c56651429a4f28d94a6483d952 <f0013046151b7467e62c471c1c83d63ea255799c"}, {"id": "8c70e6e1-5912-322f-ace8-d112f4b65c66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "a4c3cb81-cf1f-34ac-838b-2d2dc7d3fd4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25030321ba2860c56651429a4f28d94a6483d952 <abf854513bc19e6e24d45353ac99ec5627ee0acc"}, {"id": "c926c824-71cf-3fc2-a179-4283871810bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.6"}, {"id": "c9bb1b61-4486-3d9f-82b1-909d6fb1c029", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "f7cdab2d-4fe3-3395-994e-8eeb8a55ec47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cce9623e-cf45-30cd-ac23-6789ba2baa2b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}